## Use cases

- Browser or Electron log viewers whose host owns pause and history.
- Interactive Electron PTYs whose trusted host owns command execution.
- ANSI / Unicode output previews that need no process privileges.

## Accessibility

- xterm screen-reader support follows `screenReaderMode` and is on by default; a host that knows no assistive technology is running can turn it off to parse heavy output faster. Read-only output stays selectable and copyable.
- Leave `autoFocus` off unless the user explicitly opens an interactive terminal; log updates never move focus.
